function return value:
    replacement:
        @intrinsic("return", value)

function ignore value:
    replacement:
        @intrinsic("discard", value)

[an|] integer means: @intrinsic("type", "int")

[a|] {fixed integer:bits} bit integer means: @intrinsic("type", "int", bits)

[a|] {fixed integer:bits} bit floating-point number means: @intrinsic("type", "float", bits)

[a|] type means: @intrinsic("type", "type")

[a|] constraint means: @intrinsic("type", "constraint")

a value means: @intrinsic("type", "any")

fixed means: @intrinsic("fix", a value)

fixed value means: @intrinsic("fix", value)

[a|] {fixed integer:bits} bit value means: @intrinsic("type", "any", bits)

[a|] pointer to pointed means: @intrinsic("add pointer depth", pointed)

[an|] array containing {fixed integer:size} [item|items] of {type:element} means: @intrinsic("array", size, element)

value as {fixed type:destination} means: @intrinsic("cast", value, destination)

to get the captured value of {fixed:value}:
    return 1

to get the description of {a 64 bit value:value}:
    return 64

to get the description of pointer {a pointer to a value:value}:
    return 8

to get the description of pair {an array containing 2 items of a value:value}:
    return 2

to print value: ignore @intrinsic("variadic call", "libc", "printf", an integer, 1, "%d\n", value)

print the captured value of 12
print the captured value of an integer
print the description of (1 as a 64 bit integer)
print the description of (1 as a 64 bit floating-point number)
print the description of pointer "value"
print the description of pair [1, 2]
